    crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/agent/auth_method.rs:845: .expect()
    crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/agent/auth_method.rs:847: .expect()
    crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/agent/auth_method.rs:885: .expect()
    crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/agent/auth_method.rs:887: .expect()
    crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/agent/auth_method.rs:1022: .expect()
    crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/agent/auth_method.rs:1096: .expect()

Two blind spots had to be closed for that, both in `panic-site-census.py`:

- an item gated by a never-true predicate is dropped, so the sites inside it belong to no
  column; the census now folds the predicate through the same `cfg_lib.py` the guard uses.
- a `mod` declaration under such a predicate is dropped too, which means the file it names is
  compiled by nobody. Re-listing that declaration in the edge lists put the file back into a
  build and counted its sites as production; the declaration is now skipped where it is dead.

The ratchet itself still passes against the new numbers -- the crate did not acquire any new
production panic site, it just stopped being charged for sites it does not have:

    $ python3 scripts/ci/panic-site-census.py --check-baseline scripts/ci/panic-site-baseline.tsv
    baseline holds: 97 crates, 0 fewer production sites than recorded
    exit=0

    $ python3 scripts/ci/panic-site-census.py --check-uncompiled scripts/ci/uncompiled-sources.txt
    uncompiled set holds: 0 files, exactly as recorded
    exit=0


== 5. The census test that was green while measuring something else

The census fix has a fixture: a synthetic crate in which one file's only declaration sits behind
`#[cfg(any())]`, so the scanner is forced to answer "is a file whose `mod` line was dropped
compiled by anything?". The first version of that fixture was written as a flat pair of files:

    src/dropped_decl_host.rs      # contains: #[cfg(any())] mod dropped_decl;
    src/dropped_decl.rs           # the target, with a .unwrap() in it

That shape never existed in the first place. Rust resolves `mod dropped_decl;` inside
`src/dropped_decl_host.rs` to `src/dropped_decl_host/dropped_decl.rs`, so in the flat pair the
declaration named nothing, the target was already uncompiled for the "nobody declares this file"
reason the fixture separately tests with `nobody_declares.rs`, and the rule under test was
exercised by no line of the fixture. Committed as it is now:

    # scripts/ci/test-panic-site-census.py
    # The directory matters, not just the names: `mod x;` inside `src/host.rs` looks for
    # `src/host/x.rs`, so writing the pair side by side in `src/` would declare a file
    # that resolves to nothing, and the target would land in the uncompiled ledger for
    # the wrong reason -- the same reason `nobody_declares.rs` is there.
    (src / "dropped_decl_host").mkdir()
    (src / "dropped_decl_host" / "mod.rs").write_text(
        "pub fn ships_anyway() -> u32 {\n    host_side().unwrap();\n    26\n}\n\n"
        "#[cfg(any())]\nmod dropped_decl;\n",
        encoding="utf-8",
    )
    (src / "dropped_decl_host" / "dropped_decl.rs").write_text(
        "pub fn compiled_by_nobody() -> u32 {\n    dropped_decl_thing().unwrap();\n    27\n}\n",
        encoding="utf-8",
    )

The difference between the two shapes is visible by running the shipped scanner and the M13
mutant (the skip removed from `module_declarations`) against both, in one process:

    $ python3 {SCRATCH}/probe_shape.py

    == directory shape, as committed
       dropped_decl_host/dropped_decl.rs
       shipped: demo row {'unwrap': 26, 'unwrap_prod': 13, 'expect': 0, 'expect_prod': 0, 'panic': 0, 'panic_prod': 0, 'unsafe': 5, 'unsafe_prod': 4, 'unsafe_block': 2, 'unsafe_fn': 1, 'unsafe_impl': 1, 'unsafe_extern': 1, 'files': 22, 'test_files': 8, 'uncompiled_files': 2}
              uncompiled 2 files: ['dropped_decl_host/dropped_decl.rs', 'nobody_declares.rs']
              sites booked for the target file: [(2, '.unwrap()')]
       mutant : demo row {'unwrap': 27, 'unwrap_prod': 14, 'expect': 0, 'expect_prod': 0, 'panic': 0, 'panic_prod': 0, 'unsafe': 5, 'unsafe_prod': 4, 'unsafe_block': 2, 'unsafe_fn': 1, 'unsafe_impl': 1, 'unsafe_extern': 1, 'files': 22, 'test_files': 8, 'uncompiled_files': 1}
              uncompiled 1 files: ['nobody_declares.rs']
              sites booked for the target file: [(2, '.unwrap()'), (2, '.unwrap()')]

    == flat shape, the first version
       dropped_decl.rs, dropped_decl_host.rs
       shipped: demo row {'unwrap': 26, 'unwrap_prod': 13, 'expect': 0, 'expect_prod': 0, 'panic': 0, 'panic_prod': 0, 'unsafe': 5, 'unsafe_prod': 4, 'unsafe_block': 2, 'unsafe_fn': 1, 'unsafe_impl': 1, 'unsafe_extern': 1, 'files': 22, 'test_files': 8, 'uncompiled_files': 2}
              uncompiled 2 files: ['dropped_decl.rs', 'nobody_declares.rs']
