The name-level accounting, `mod tests` before and after (module bodies diffed by the `fn` names
following each `#[test]`):

    23 parked            8 kept under the same name
                         3 back under a new name, because the claim changed shape
                        11 deleted, each named in the module doc with what it asserted
                         1 folded into a loop over every cached-token input
    -> 14 in `mod tests` = 8 + 3 + 3 written for this batch
    -> 20 in the file   = 14 + 4 in `runtime_api_key_tests` + 2 in `chaos_auth_tests`

The three renames are `disable_api_key_auth_suppresses_xai_api_key_method` to
`disable_api_key_auth_decides_the_predicate_not_the_advertised_list`,
`grok_login_legacy_token_does_not_require_login` to
`legacy_grok_auth_env_is_loaded_but_never_advertised`, and
`no_legacy_token_means_no_cached_token_advertised` to `no_legacy_token_means_no_current_credential`.
The new tests are `retained_login_methods_still_build`, which is where
`auth_provider_command_sets_external_provider_meta`'s assertion moved to when the advertised list
stopped being reachable, `push_interactive_login_selects_the_configured_method`, and
